  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Primary">Primary Inference Model</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Name">Model name</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Url">URL(OpenAI format)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Api">API</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.DocsNote">Please refer to the official documentation for the information above.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Advanced">Advanced settings</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.AdvancedNote">Open the advanced settings window to configure parameters such as the AI model's prompts, temperature, and maximum context length. It is not recommended for users without sufficient understanding to make adjustments here.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.AdvancedTitle">Advanced settings</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.AdvancedPending">The parameter window is not implemented yet.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.LocalModel">Small local model</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.LocalModelName">qwen2.5:7b</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.LocalModelNone">No local model installed</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.LocalModelNote">This software includes various features and privacy controls that rely on local models. Uninstalling them frees up hardware resources, which is not recommended. If your hardware is not well suited to the installed model, run Check to get a recommendation for this machine.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Check">Check</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.CheckTitle">Check</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.CheckPending">Hardware detection and model recommendation are not implemented yet.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Delete">Delete</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.DeleteTitle">Remove the local model?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.DeleteBody">The local model will be removed and the features that rely on it will fall back until you install one again.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Ollama">I have custom local models, using Ollama</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.OllamaNote">If you configure local models through Ollama, open the small window to do it; the built-in small models are then removed to free up space. To keep them and simply add Ollama models, use the button below instead.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Add">Add custom models and services</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.AddTitle">Add custom models and services</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.AddPending">The model and service window is not implemented yet.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Dialog.Ok">OK</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Dialog.Delete">Delete</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.OllamaTitle">Using Ollama</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.OllamaAddress">Address (fixed)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.OllamaModelLabel">Model name</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.OllamaWindowNote">The address is fixed because the Ollama path is the advanced option. Enabling it removes the bundled local model to free disk space; to add a model in addition, use “Add custom models and services”.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.OllamaEnable">Enable Ollama</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Installing">Installing the bundled model…</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.Downloading">Downloading</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.GpuLabel">Hardware acceleration (Vulkan)</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.GpuOn">On</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.GpuOff">Off (CPU)</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.GpuNoteOn">Runs on the GPU (Vulkan). If the model does not fit, lower the offload in the advanced settings.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.GpuNoteOff">Runs on the CPU. On a supported graphics card this is roughly 4x slower.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.CloudSaved">Saved and active</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.CloudSavedShort">Primary model saved</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Model.CloudNotConfigured">Not configured: the local model answers</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Header">Email retrieval</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Note">By default the daily fetch reads the copy Thunderbird keeps on this machine. Manual accounts (below) are an advanced option for setups Thunderbird cannot handle.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Add">Add an account</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Address">Address</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Server">IMAP server / port</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Secret">App password</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Days">Look back</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.UnreadOnly">Unread only</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.AddButton">Add</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Import">Import from Thunderbird</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Test">Test</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Remove">Remove</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Web.Header">Website browsing</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Web.Note">Pages the daily fetch reads. Only GET is used; forms are never submitted. Cookies for signed-in sites come from the browser cookie plugin, which asks for each domain separately.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Web.Add">Add page</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Web.Remove">Remove</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Web.Watermark">https://…</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Thunderbird">Read mail from Thunderbird</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.ThunderbirdNote">Sign in to your mailbox in Thunderbird once; the daily fetch reads the copy Thunderbird keeps on this machine. No server address, no app password, no protocol setup — which is why it works for mailboxes that refuse everything else.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.UseThunderbird">Use Thunderbird</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Rescan">Scan again</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="Settings.Email.Advanced">Advanced: configure a server by hand (not recommended)</x:String>

  <!--
    English UI text. Every key here must also exist in Lang.zh.axaml —
    tools/CogniCustos.Ui.Tests compares the two files and fails on a mismatch.
    Translators: copy this file, rename it to Lang.<culture>.axaml, translate the
    values, keep the keys untouched.
  -->

